                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-text mb-3">US Sports League: Protecting Minors' Data</h2>

                <p class="text-brand-muted mb-6 leading-relaxed flex-grow">
                    <strong>The Challenge:</strong> A US professional sports league with a nationwide youth club
                    network, and rigid data lake pipelines, needed to onboard its entire under-18 membership base.
                    Under strict legal constraints, marketing had to reach parents and guardians without exposing any
                    minor's personal data.
                    <br><br>
                    <strong>My Solution:</strong> Led the technical discovery with their data engineers and
                    structured their data sources with them. I designed the account's identity resolution and a
                    "Parent/Guardian" entity model in the CDP that routed all communications to authorised adults while
                    keeping the non-adult profile data siloed for analysis only.
                    <br><br>
                    <strong>The Outcome:</strong> The model was signed off by the client's own data-protection and
                    engineering teams and shipped, letting them reach the guardian audience without minors' personal
                    data leaving the analytics silo.
                </p>

